The spirit world closed in around them. They were confronted by Big Black Bear while they were still in the boat. The bear announced that it was the guardian of the river and that they had three choices: to become the bear's slaves, to leave the river and never return, or to die. The young men chose the second option and left the river. 
On their way back to the village they came across a young woman who was lost.  She was the spirit of the mist, who had been separated from her husband the spirit of the river.  She offered the young men a chance to help her rejoin her husband, in exchange for great rewards.  The young men agreed and so traveled back to the river, where they successfully reunited the spirit of the river and the spirit of the mist.  The bear was surprised and allowed them to pass.
The young men returned to the village, where they were welcomed as heroes.  The woman grew to become the young man's wife, and they lived happily ever after.


