Suddenly they heard the noise of a great waterfall. They thought it was impossible to have a waterfall in such a calm and foggy night, but they followed the noise and found themselves in the middle of a very large waterfall. It was the St. Lawrence River rushing over the Shannon Falls, which they had never seen before. The next day they went back and saw that it was actually three waterfalls, the others being the Long Sault and the rapids of the Saint Lawrence. They were astonished that such a huge waterfall could exist without rain or a hurricane. They named the falls "Niagara" after the Native American word for "thunderous water".

